{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":46228,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"62ffce68ae99520e9cffb854de92c4435a461cc4da54ff3ed828ba07485af998","packTokens":16599,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":1,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":255,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":384,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1731,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":2,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":4849,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":9263,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-13T12:23:34.269Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261013-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-1d97\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"auth\",\n  \"payments\",\n  \"pii\",\n  \"migration\",\n  \"public-api\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": false\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"The product stories describe behaviors beyond the locked API contract, while the final instruction says to implement the contract exactly. When a story requires behavior the contract does not define, which scope should govern?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only operations and behavior defined by the locked OpenAPI contract; do not add uncontracted behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For sample rows that refer to one another, should the seeder create compatible references, or may it seed each table independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create compatible references between related sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"The contract includes an operation to return a configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, but the provider and source of that configuration are not identified here. What should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider and supply its authorization URL and token-validation settings through deployment configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When demo seeding is disabled and a database table has no records, should list operations return an empty list or provide sample rows without persisting them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return an empty list when the database has no matching records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The staff identity-provider URL and token-validation settings will come from deployment configuration. What should happen if required settings are missing or invalid?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail application startup with a clear configuration error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Apply a reviewed database migration during deployment, preserving existing data; use EnsureCreated only for genuinely empty databases.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should schema changes be applied to databases that already exist when the new persistent tables are introduced?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Have deployment provision the initial account outside the API; do not add an API bootstrap flow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With demo seeding disabled, how should the first PostgreSQL account be made available so the API can authorize callers?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Identify the organization's existing staff provider and supply its authorization URL and validation settings; do not introduce a new provider.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which staff identity provider and concrete authorization-URL and token-validation settings should the API use?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Provide valid nonproduction settings for the chosen provider through test and factory configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the test and factory runs obtain the valid nonproduction identity-provider settings required for startup?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Keep behavior limited to the locked contract; use standard secure password hashing for stored passwords, and do not add new lockout or one-time-code policies.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How much customer-authentication behavior beyond the locked contract should be specified for failed logins and password storage?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Match the token's email claim to the account email, and deny access when no matching enabled account exists.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Which token claim should identify the PostgreSQL staff account, and what should happen if a valid token has no matching or has a disabled account?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"For a stock collection request whose filter names a warehouse outside the caller’s scope, what should the API return?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return 200 OK with an empty list, applying the caller’s scope to the results.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authorization include a separate role-to-operation permission table beyond the roles and scopes stated in the locked contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not add a separate role-to-operation table; enforce only the role and scope restrictions stated by the locked contract.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"How should startup determine whether a database qualifies for EnsureCreated, given that existing databases must use the reviewed deployment migration?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use EnsureCreated only when the database has no tables; otherwise leave schema changes to the reviewed deployment migration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 3,\n     \"lineStart\": 1,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/App.Api.csproj\",\n     \"quote\": \"<Project Sdk=\\\"Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web\\\">\\n  <PropertyGroup>\\n    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>\",\n     \"symbol\": \"App.Api project\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 5,\n     \"lineStart\": 4,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);\\nbuilder.Services.AddOpenApi();\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program startup\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 27,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.UseCors();\\napp.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-1\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The existing API is an ASP.NET Core .NET 9 project. Its startup registers OpenAPI and currently exposes a root health response plus OpenAPI and Swagger UI; this is an API shell rather than an implementation of the portal operations.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 12,\n     \"lineStart\": 1,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"openapi: 3.0.3\\ninfo:\\n  title: Meridian Cold Chain API\\n  version: 1.0.0\\n  description: \\\"Shared contract for the Meridian responsive web portal.\\\"\\nservers:\\n  - url: /api\\npaths:\\n  /auth/staff/authorization-url:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: getStaffAuthorizationUrl\\n      summary: \\\"Get the configured staff identity-provider authorization URL.\\\"\",\n     \"symbol\": \"OpenAPI paths\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 164,\n     \"lineStart\": 144,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /warehouse/receipts:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: listReceipts\\n      summary: \\\"List warehouse-