.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-8\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-8\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The API configures CORS for `Cors:Origin` (defaulting to `http://localhost:3000`) and its registered UI is Swagger at `/swagger`, backed by `/openapi/v1.json`; no portal screens are part of the current API behavior.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-13T12:24:54.144Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261013-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-1d97\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"Route mappings/controllers/handlers in App.Api/**/*.cs: MapGet, MapPost, MapPut, MapPatch, MapDelete, HttpGet, HttpPost, HttpPut, HttpPatch, HttpDelete; found only the root health route.\",\n    \"Contract paths and operationIds in contracts/openapi.yaml; found the specified operations, but no implementation mappings in the API source.\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"DbSet declarations and entity/model classes in App.Api/**/*.cs; found only an empty AppDb context and no entity sets.\",\n    \"Database read/write logic in App.Api/**/*.cs; found only PostgreSQL setup and EnsureCreated startup logic.\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"Route mappings/controllers/handlers in App.Api/**/*.cs for the contract operations; found only the root health route.\",\n    \"Customer order operation in contracts/openapi.yaml; found changeCustomerOrder, but no corresponding API handler.\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"Seed:Demo and SeedData.Run in App.Api; found the startup gate and an empty Run method.\",\n    \"Sample/example blocks in contracts/openapi.yaml; found response examples but no corresponding sample-row inserts in SeedData.cs.\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Every operation and response case defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, including contract-valid and contract-invalid requests and the declared authentication and authorization cases.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status, content type, response fields, and error body conform to that operation's OpenAPI request and response definitions.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test client sends the corresponding HTTP requests to every declared operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A caller authenticated as an account with assigned warehouse or organization scopes calls a collection or record operation using contract-defined filters.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and returned list or record contain only data within the caller's assigned scope and reflect the supplied filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller sends the HTTP request to that operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is running with valid startup configuration.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status for each request is 200.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client requests `GET /`, `GET /openapi/v1.json`, and `GET /swagger`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 12,\n     \"lineStart\": 1,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"openapi: 3.0.3\\ninfo:\\n  title: Meridian Cold Chain API\\n  version: 1.0.0\\n  description: \\\"Shared contract for the Meridian responsive web portal.\\\"\\nservers:\\n  - url: /api\\npaths:\\n  /auth/staff/authorization-url:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: getStaffAuthorizationUrl\\n      summary: \\\"Get the configured staff identity-provider authorization URL.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement only the operations and behavior defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, with the existing root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes retained.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"When a contract operation creates or changes business data, the Meridian API shall persist the resulting records in the PostgreSQL database configured by `ConnectionStrings:App`, apply only lifecycle constraints explicitly described by that operation in the contract, use `EnsureCreated` only when the database has no tables, and leave schema changes for a reviewed deployment migration that preserves existing data in databases that already have tables.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 162,\n     \"lineEnd\": 183,\n     \"quote\": \"    post:\\n      operationId: createReceipt\\n      summary: \\\"Record and quarantine an inbound receipt.\\\"\\n      requestBody:\\n        required: true\\n        content:\\n          application/json:\\n            schema:\\n              $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/ReceiptInput\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/RecordResult\\\"\\n        \\\"400\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/BadRequest\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"409\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Conflict\\\"\\n        \\\"500\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/ServerError\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 1124,\n     \"lineEnd\": 1149,\n     \"quote\": \"    patch:\\n      operationId: changeCustomerOrder\\n      summary: \\\"Change a customer order before packing.\\\"\\n      parameters:\\n        - $ref: \\\"#/components/parameters/OrderId\\\"\\n      requestBody:\\n        required: true\\n        content:\\n          application/json:\\n            schema:\\n              $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/OrderInput\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/RecordResult\\\"\\n        \\\"400\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/BadRequest\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"404\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/NotFound\\\"\\n        \\\"409\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Conflict\\\"\\n        \\\"500\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/ServerError\\\"\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"Q-14\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid request to a contract operation that creates or changes persistent business data.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls the operation and then reads the affected entity through the corresponding contract operation or directly from the database.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the operation's contract-declared success status, the returned record identifier and values reflect the requested change, and the persisted row values match that change.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid receipt input.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls `POST /api/warehouse/receipts` and reads the resulting receipt.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the returned record status is Quarantined, and the persisted row status is Quarantined.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A customer-owned order that is before packing and a valid order change input.\",\n     \"when\": \"The authenticated customer sends a valid `PATCH /api/customer/orders/{orderId}` request.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, and the returned record and persisted row reflect the change.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n     \"given\": \"An existing PostgreSQL database contains existing records and a reviewed migration introduces the required schema changes.\",\n     \"when\": \"The deployment migration runs against that database.\",\n     \"then\": \"The existing row values remain unchanged and the database table list contains the migrated schema.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.5\",\n     \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has no tables.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and a client requests `GET /`.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the database table list contains the contract-backed tables.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.6\",\n     \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has at least one table and existing records, and a reviewed migration is pending.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts before the deployment migration runs and a client requests `GET /`.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, existing row values remain unchanged, and the database table list matches its pre-start list.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database, valid staff identity-provider settings, and `Seed:Demo` set to true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and a client requests `GET /`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public static class SeedData\\n{\\n    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 2585,\n     \"lineStart\": 2575,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"          example:\\n            items:\\n              - id: 3101\\n                name: \\\"Cedar Clinic receipt\\\"\\n                status: \\\"Quarantined\\\"\\n                productName: \\\"Vaccine Pack\\\"\\n                lotNumber: \\\"LOT-2026-041\\\"\\n                expiryDate: \\\"2027-06-30\\\"\\n                quantity: 24\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the `Seed:Demo` setting is true, the Meridian API shall run `SeedData.Run` during startup.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An empty database with its contract-backed tables created.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The row count in each contract-backed table is between two and five, the rows are based on contract examples, and each relationship field value resolves to a row in its referenced table.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test directly invokes the public `SeedData.Run` method with `AppDb`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A database with at least one contract-backed table already containing records and other contract-backed tables empty.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The existing row values remain unchanged and the row count in that populated table does not increase.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test directly invokes the public `SeedData.Run` method with `AppDb`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public static class SeedData\\n{\\n    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When `SeedData.Run` is called, the Meridian Cold Chain API shall add between two and five contract-example-based rows only to each empty contract-backed table, preserve existing rows, and create references that resolve to existing related rows.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database containing a non-demo account row provisioned by deployment and no rows matching the contract's demo examples, with valid staff identity-provider settings and `Seed:Demo` false or unset.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The provisioned account row values remain unchanged and the row count matching each contract demo example remains zero.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If `Seed:Demo` is false or unset, then the Meridian API shall not run the demo seeder or create demo rows.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has no matching persisted records for a contract collection operation and `Seed:Demo` is false.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the contract-declared success status, the returned list count is 0, and the database row count remains zero.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls that collection operation.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a contract collection operation has no matching persisted records, then the Meridian API shall return an empty list rather than unpersisted sample records.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Valid deployment configuration for the organization's existing staff identity provider, including its authorization URL and token-validation settings.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response field `message` contains the configured authorization URL.\",\n     \"when\": \"A caller sends `GET /api/auth/staff/authorization-url`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Valid settings for the organization's existing staff identity provider and a caller with permission to access a protected contract operation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The valid-token response status is the contract-declared success status and the invalid-token response status is 401.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller sends one request with a valid provider token and one with an invalid provider token.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Test and factory configurations provide valid nonproduction authorization URL and token-validation settings for the organization's existing staff identity provider.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response field contains the configured nonproduction authorization URL.\",\n     \"when\": \"The test or factory host starts and a client calls `GET /api/auth/staff/authorization-url`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API and its test and factory configurations shall use the organization's existing staff identity provider, obtain its authorization URL and token-validation settings from deployment configuration, and use valid nonproduction settings in test and factory runs.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"Q-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Deployment configuration with a required staff identity-provider setting missing or invalid.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The process exit status is nonzero and the startup error identifies the configuration problem.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process starts.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A required staff identity-provider authorization URL or token-validation setting is missing or invalid.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The process exit status is nonzero and the startup error identifies the affected setting.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application host starts with that deployment configuration.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The existing `HealthTests.ApiIsUp` and factory checks run with valid nonproduction staff identity-provider authorization URL and token-validation settings.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The process exit status is 0 and the response status for each request is 200.\",\n     \"when\": \"The test and factory hosts start and clients request `GET /`, `GET /openapi/v1.json`, and `GET /swagger`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a required staff identity-provider authorization URL or token-validation setting is missing or invalid, then the Meridian API shall fail application startup with an error identifying the affected setting; the existing `HealthTests.ApiIsUp` and factory checks use valid nonproduction settings and continue to reach the health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement customer and staff authentication and authorization only through the locked contract, store customer passwords using a standard salted password-hashing algorithm rather than as plaintext, authorize callers only using the roles and scopes stated in the contract without a separate role-to-operation permission table, match staff token email claims to enabled account emails, deny access for unmatched or disabled accounts, and add no lockout or one-time-code policies beyond the contract.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"lineEnd\": 40,\n     \"quote\": \"  /auth/customer/sign-in:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: signInCustomer\\n      summary: \\\"Submit customer email and password and begin one-time-code verification.\\\"\\n      requestBody:\\n        required: true\\n        content:\\n          application/json:\\n            schema:\\n              $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/Credentials\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/AuthResult\\\"\\n        \\\"400\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/BadRequest\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"500\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/ServerError\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 2535,\n     \"lineEnd\": 2567,\n     \"quote\": \"    AccountInput:\\n      type: object\\n      required:\\n        - fullName\\n        - email\\n        - roles\\n      properties:\\n        fullName:\\n          type: string\\n        email:\\n          type: string\\n          format: email\\n        roles:\\n          type: array\\n          items:\\n            type: string\\n            enum:\\n              - Driver\\n              - Dispatcher\\n              - Quality Officer\\n              - Quality Manager\\n              - Auditor\\n              - System Administrator\\n              - Customer Administrator\\n              - Customer\\n        warehouseIds:\\n          type: array\\n          items:\\n            type: integer\\n        organizationIds:\\n          type: array\\n          items:\\n            type: integer\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 1650,\n     \"lineEnd\": 1685,\n     \"quote\": \"  /admin/accounts:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: listAccounts\\n      summary: \\\"List accounts, roles and access scope.\\\"\\n      parameters:\\n        - $ref: \\\"#/components/parameters/Search\\\"\\n        - $ref: \\\"#/components/parameters/Status\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Collection\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"500\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/ServerError\\\"\\n    post:\\n      operationId: createAccount\\n      summary: \\\"Create an account and assign its roles and access scope.\\\"\\n      requestBody:\\n        required: true\\n        content:\\n          application/json:\\n            schema:\\n              $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/AccountInput\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/RecordResult\\\"\\n        \\\"400\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/BadRequest\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"409\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Conflict\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"lineStart\": 1036,\n     \"lineEnd\": 1060,\n     \"quote\": \"  /quality/recalls/{recallId}/write-offs:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: writeOffRecallRemainder\\n      summary: \\\"Submit a signed Quality Manager write-off for unaccounted recall quantity.\\\"\\n      parameters:\\n        - $ref: \\\"#/components/parameters/RecallId\\\"\\n      requestBody:\\n        required: true\\n        content:\\n          application/json:\\n            schema:\\n              $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/WriteOffInput\\\"\\n      responses:\\n        \\\"200\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/RecordResult\\\"\\n        \\\"400\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/BadRequest\\\"\\n        \\\"401\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\\\"\\n        \\\"403\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Forbidden\\\"\\n        \\\"404\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/NotFound\\\"\\n        \\\"409\\\":\\n          $ref: \\\"#/components/responses/Conflict\\\"\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-10\",\n    \"Q-11\",\n    \"Q-12\",\n    \"Q-13\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A valid staff token associated with an enabled PostgreSQL account whose `warehouseIds` contains only 10; persisted stock rows exist in warehouses 10 and 20.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller requests the stock collection with `warehouseId=20`.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"given\": \"An existing customer account with credentials accepted by the contracted sign-in operation, a valid one-time code available for that account, an associated PostgreSQL account record assigned organization 10, and persisted orders for organizations 10 and 20.\",\n     \"when\": \"The customer submits credentials to `POST /api/auth/customer/sign-in`, submits the issued challenge and valid code to `POST /api/auth/customer/code/verify`, then lists orders and requests an order belonging to organization 20.\",\n     \"then\": \"The sign-in and code-verification response statuses are 200, the response list contains only organization-10 records, and the response status for the organization-20 order is 403.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n     \"given\": \"Two authenticated staff identities with associated PostgreSQL account records assigned Quality Officer and Quality Manager roles, respectively, and the same permitted quality scope; an open recall has an unaccounted quantity.\",\n     \"when\": \"Each account submits the contract's signed `POST /api/quality/recalls/{recallId}/write-offs` operation for that recall.\",\n     \"then\": \"The Quality Officer response status is 403 and the Quality Manager response status is 200.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A customer account password is set through a contract-defined password-setting operation.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test reads the corresponding PostgreSQL account row and verifies the stored password value against the submitted password.\",\n     \"then\": \"The row's password field contains a salted password hash that verifies against the submitted password and does not equal the plaintext password.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A valid staff identity-provider token has an email claim matching an enabled PostgreSQL account assigned permission to use a protected contract operation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller sends the token with a request to that operation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the operation's contract-declared success status.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.6\",\n     \"given\": \"A valid staff identity-provider token has no matching PostgreSQL account email, or matches a disabled account.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller sends the token with a request to a protected contract operation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 403.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A newly deployed PostgreSQL database has no account row and the deployment has the initial account details.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"The PostgreSQL account row list contains the provisioned initial account.\",\n     \"when\": \"The deployment provisions the initial account.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian deployment shall provision the initial PostgreSQL account outside the API rather than through an API bootstrap flow.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Portal screens and web-app implementation (I-5, Q-1).\",\n  \"Product-story behavior that is not defined by the locked OpenAPI contract (Q-1).\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-1: For this specification, “a few” sample rows means between two and five rows per empty contract-backed table.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}